          ],
          "content": "(i) $2 . 0 \\times 1 0 ^ { 2 3 }$ seconds"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.125,
            0.417,
            0.144
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $6 . 2 5 \\times 1 0 ^ { 2 2 }$ seconds"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.167,
            0.276,
            0.186
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 43"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.195,
            0.605,
            0.217
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ What does the first part of each name denote?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.22,
            0.847,
            0.258
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** The first part of each name denotes the number of times 1000s are multiplied to 1000."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.279,
            0.314,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 44–45**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.319,
            0.294,
            0.343
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.35,
            0.765,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": "1. Find out the units digit in the value of $2^{224} \\div 4^{32} ?$ [Hint: 4 = 2<sup>2</sup>]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.375,
            0.405,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** The units digit is $^ { \\circ } 6 ^ { \\prime }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.405,
            0.847,
            0.444
          ],
          "content": "2. There are 5 bottles in a container. Every day, a new container is brought in. How many bottles would be there after 40 days?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.449,
            0.404,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** $2 0 0 = 2 \\times 1 0 ^ { 2 }$ bottles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.478,
            0.847,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": "3. Write the given number as the product of two or more powers in three different ways. The powers can be any integers. (i) $6 4 ^ { 3 }$ (ii) $1 9 2 ^ { 8 }$ (iii) $3 2 ^ { - 5 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.547,
            0.419,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Some of the ways are"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.564,
            0.453,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": "(i) $2^{10} \\times 2^{8}, \\quad 4^{5} \\times 4^{4}, \\quad 8^{3} \\times 8^{3}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.587,
            0.432,
            0.624
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $2^{48} \\times 3^{8}, \\left | 2^{40} \\times \\bar{2}^{8} \\times 3^{8} \\right.$ $2 ^ { 4 0 } \\times 6 ^ { 8 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.18,
            0.629,
            0.501,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $2^{-10} \\times 2^{-15}, 2^{-5} \\times 2^{-20}, 4^{-12} \\times 2^{-1}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.661,
            0.846,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": "4. Examine each statement below and find out if it is ‘Always True’, ‘Only Sometimes True’, or ‘Never True’. Explain your reasoning."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.699,
            0.63,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": "(i) Cube numbers are also square numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.717,
            0.631,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Fourth powers are also square numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.735,
            0.847,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "(iii) The fifth power of a number is divisible by the cube of that number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.772,
            0.744,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": "(iv) The product of two cube numbers is a cube number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.79,
            0.833,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": "(v) $q ^ { 4 6 }$ is both a 4th power and a 6th power (q is a prime number) **Ans:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.833,
            0.452,
            0.85
          ],
          "content": "(i) Only Sometimes True."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.85,
            0.773,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": "“This is only true for numbers that have powers as $6 . ^ { \\flat }$ $n ^ { 6 }   = ( n ^ { 2 } ) ^ { 3 } = ( n ^ { 3 } ) ^ { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.919,
            0.141,
            0.939
          ],
          "content": "6"
        }
      ]
    }
